  "authorNotes": "Showdown / race, 2-4 players, everyone spawns together on the start dock. Two gaps, same reach budgets as the campaign (swing-race-a 260px, rope-race-b 300px), plus one shared hazard: gate-crusher patrols the middle pier's doorway on a y650-850 path at 130px/s, fast enough to matter and identical for every racer — nobody can hog or disable it, so it stays fair. No assist beams — Showdown is a contest, not a tutorial. goal.requires is 'any': the instant one player's head crosses the goal shape the round ends, matching §8.2's 'first to the goal wins'. relic-w4-a sits on the middle pier as an optional detour for the haul/flawless objectives, which score independently of who wins the round (§7's per-player scoring, not the win condition)."
